{
  "_about": "Earned nicknames (release 2; Brian's yes of 23 November 2026 12:05Z, idea 2: 'a division that wins several hard fights earns a nickname that shows on its flag'). The grand campaign's flag 'nicknames' (stage.json), set as a campaign opens; off, nothing here is read and every war is the war without it. A hard fight is a battle won against the odds or at a price: an attack carried at odds of 'attackOdds' or less, a line held against odds of 'holdOdds' or more, or either won while losing 'bloody' of the corps' men or more. An attack at 'walkover' odds or better is never hard. A corps that has won 'need' hard fights, and has no name yet, is given one by its own army, in its nation's own style ('nations' -> 'styles'; a nation not listed takes '_default'), so long as fewer than 'most' of that nation's corps in the field carry a name. A name gives no edge in battle: it is a name on a flag and in the record, for every nation alike. Every name is our own: none is a real formation's nickname or a name from any other game, and 'blocked' lists the real nicknames that a test keeps out of every list.",
